<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Errors in multiplication Q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A groundskeeper is preparing to measure a football pitch for an upcoming match. Using a measuring wheel, the length is recorded as \({@length@}\) m and the width as \({@width@}\) m, both correct to the nearest metre.</p>
<p>(a) Find the maximum possible length of the pitch.</p>
 <p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Find the minimum possible length of the pitch.</p>
 <p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) Find the maximum possible width of the pitch.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>(d) Find the minimum possible width of the pitch.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p>(e) Using the recorded length and width, calculate the working area of the pitch. Then, using your answers to (a) and (c), calculate the maximum possible area. Hence find the absolute error in the area.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</p>
<p>(f) Find the relative error in the area.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]</p>
<p>(g) Find the percentage error in the area.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt7]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution.</h3>
<p>The pitch length was recorded as {@length@} m and the width as {@width@} m, both correct to the nearest metre.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Maximum possible length:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Max length} = {@length@} + {@length_err@} = {@max_length@} \text{ m} \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Minimum possible length:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Min length} = {@length@} - {@length_err@} = {@min_length@} \text{ m} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Maximum possible width:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Max width} = {@width@} + {@width_err@} = {@max_width@} \text{ m} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>Minimum possible width:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Min width} = {@width@} - {@width_err@} = {@min_width@} \text{ m} \]</p>

<p>(e) <strong>Working area and absolute error:</strong></p>
<p>Using the recorded measurements:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Working area} = {@length@} \times {@width@} = {@W_area@} \text{ m}^2 \]</p>
<p>Using the maximum length and maximum width:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Maximum area} = {@max_length@} \times {@max_width@} = {@max_area@} \text{ m}^2 \]</p>
<p>\[ \text{Absolute error} = \text{Maximum area} - \text{Working area} = {@max_area@} - {@W_area@} = {@ta1@} \text{ m}^2 \]</p>

<p>(f) <strong>Relative error:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Relative error} = \frac{\text{Absolute error}}{\text{Working area}} = \frac{{@ta1@}}{{@W_area@}} \approx {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(g) <strong>Percentage error:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Percentage error} = \text{Relative error} \times 100\% = {@ta2@} \times 100\% \approx {@ta3@}\% \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
